\newlabel{tab:e4_results}{{XIV}{22}{Extension~4 results: SAC multi-target state generalisation on SiliQun \texttt {simos\_nominal} profile ($n=3$ qubits, 3 seeds: 42, 123, 456). Reward weights are optimised via Bayesian search; no target-specific tuning. $\bar {F}\pm \sigma $ = mean $\pm $ std across 3 seeds; 95\% CI = $\bar {F}\pm 1.96\,\sigma /\sqrt {3}$. Hardware: RTX~2070 8\,GB VRAM; wall-clock $\approx $1.5\,h}{table.14}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Extension~4 results summary. \textbf  {(a)} Mean best fidelity $\bar  {F}_\text  {best}$ per target state (bars: mean; error bars: $\pm \sigma $; dots: individual seed values). The dashed red line marks the $F \geq 0.99$ threshold. GHZ-3 and Bell-3 exceed the threshold across all three seeds; W-3 plateaus at $\bar  {F} = 0.8551$, below the threshold. \textbf  {(b)} Steps to best fidelity per seed. Seed~456 converges in 9{,}209 steps for GHZ/Bell, roughly $6\times $ faster than seeds 42 and 123. W-state runs exhaust the full $5\times 10^5$ step budget (marked $\times $). Hardware: RTX~2070 Max-Q 8\,GB VRAM.}}{22}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:e4_results}{{10}{22}{Extension~4 results summary. \textbf {(a)} Mean best fidelity $\bar {F}_\text {best}$ per target state (bars: mean; error bars: $\pm \sigma $; dots: individual seed values). The dashed red line marks the $F \geq 0.99$ threshold. GHZ-3 and Bell-3 exceed the threshold across all three seeds; W-3 plateaus at $\bar {F} = 0.8551$, below the threshold. \textbf {(b)} Steps to best fidelity per seed. Seed~456 converges in 9{,}209 steps for GHZ/Bell, roughly $6\times $ faster than seeds 42 and 123. W-state runs exhaust the full $5\times 10^5$ step budget (marked $\times $). Hardware: RTX~2070 Max-Q 8\,GB VRAM}{figure.10}{}}
